  "conformance": {
    "streams": "63 seed/stream/position combinations, five sequential draws alternating shared handles, plus a 1,048,833-field two-batch case; exact CPU fields and word positions match",
    "boundaries": "All-zero/all-ones/incrementing seeds; stream identifiers 0, 7 and u64::MAX; odd offsets, ChaCha block/buffer edges, 32-bit block-counter carry and near stream exhaustion",
    "rejection": "Forced p-1, p, p+1, u64::MAX, zero and one across 1/255/256/257/4097 candidate lengths and offsets 0/1/15, including all-rejected tiles; GPU compaction matches the actual CPU field sampler",
    "trace_commitments": "Base and cubic traces at 1/8/256/8192 rows, widths crossing transform tiles, two sequential shared-stream commitments per shape; CPU matrices, caps, salts and authentication paths match",
    "quotient_commitments": "2/4/16 chunks at 8/32/64/8192 rows per chunk and shifts 7/11; sequential random-column and independent-mask samples match CPU hiding commitments and paths",
    "rejections": "Zero/oversized/over-budget draws preserve cursor and allocation baseline; foreign-session and wrong-count samples reject before commitment allocations/uploads",
    "failure": "Injected execution failure after a completed random batch retires all shared handles and releases private output/scratch; exhaustion rejects rather than wrapping",
    "cleanup": "Explicit generated-buffer scrub reads back zero; all native checks drain to zero managed bytes and release their lease",
    "proof_regressions": "Existing full/compact device-input proofs retain exact CPU bytes and unchanged verification; registered witness proofs and debug CPU audits still pass. Those proof entry points still use CPU random expansion."
